A column the table has already, filled where it is NULL: a step is plain
SQL, so it may update any rows. It runs once; the rows it left alone keep
their values.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Pea Soup', NULL), (2, 'Rye Bread', 'bread');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT) STRICT;

== ledger
UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-')) WHERE slug IS NULL;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, ledger.sql's step 1
  step 1
    UPDATE dish SET slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-')) WHERE slug IS NULL;

== query
SELECT id, slug FROM dish ORDER BY id

